[38;5;246m  ⎿  · How should the app determine which environment it's running in? → Hostname detection (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Hostname detection it is.

  Next fork: [1mhow [38;5;153msettings.js[39m gets into [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.[0m This matters beyond style — it decides whether [38;5;153mindex.html[39m changes,
  whether you can still open the page as a [38;5;153mfile://[39m URL, and whether the settings module is reachable from the Node side
  of the repo.

  - [1mPlain global script[0m — [38;5;153m<script src="settings.js">[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m; settings exposes one global (e.g. [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS[39m).
    Matches [38;5;153mapp.js[39m exactly as written today (it's already global-scope script code). Keeps [38;5;153mfile://[39m working. Costs: adds
    a global, and load order in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes load-bearing.
  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m does [38;5;153mimport { apiEndpoint } from [39m
    [38;5;153m'./settings.js'[39m. Properly scoped, explicit dependency, no ordering hazard. Costs: [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m is fetched under
    CORS rules, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly from disk stops working — you'd need a local server for dev.

  [1mMy recommendation: plain global script.[0m It's what the existing file already is, it adds no dev-workflow requirement,
  and the repo has nothing else pulling it toward modules. The ES-module version is the better long-term shape, but it's
  a change to how you run the page locally, which is a real cost to pay for one config value. Either way [38;5;153mapp.js[39m ends up
  reading a named settings value, so switching later is a small, contained edit.

  Note on the CommonJS [38;5;153msrc/[39m half: neither option makes [38;5;153msettings.js[39m usable from [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m without a bundler. I'm
  treating the settings module as browser-side only unless you tell me the Node side needs it too.
